---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Janghan (장한, 1927) — Digitizing a Kisaeng Magazine"
  description="Building a machine-readable corpus of Janghan (장한), the 1927 magazine written by kisaeng — OCR correction, Hanja-mixed tokenization, and provenance tracking."
>
  <section class="band container">
    <p class="caption-mono-sm rise">Status: corpus building</p>
    <h1 class="display-md rise rise-2">Janghan (장한, 1927)</h1>

    <div class="prose lede">
      <p class="body-lg rise rise-3">
        In 1927, kisaeng in Seoul published a magazine of their own: Janghan (장한).
        This project is building a machine-readable corpus of it — a digitization
        effort, page by page, so that the magazine can be read, searched, and cited
        as data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><hr class="hr" /></div>

  <section class="band container reveal">
    <h2 class="display-sm">Method</h2>
    <div class="prose section-body">
      <p class="body-md">
        Colonial-period Korean print is hard on machines: vertical layouts, Hanja-mixed
        script, and inconsistent typography defeat off-the-shelf OCR. The pipeline here
        pairs OCR correction with Hanja-aware tokenization, and every text carries
        provenance — which page, which scan, which correction pass — so the corpus
        stays auditable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><hr class="hr" /></div>

  <section class="band container reveal">
    <a class="pill" href="/projects">All projects →</a>
  </section>

  <style>
    .lede {
      margin-top: var(--s-2xl);
    }

    .section-body {
      margin-top: var(--s-lg);
    }

    .section-body p {
      margin: 0;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
